# D18. Every direct module this tree may depend on, one path per line. The gate
# diffs the module graph against this file, so taking a new dependency is a
# visible change here rather than a line in go.mod nobody reads.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# The parent proposal's table says why each one is not the standard library.
#
# An entry here is a module the tree actually imports. Listing one it does not
# makes the gate fail closed on a dependency nobody took.

golang.org/x/sys

# Hanami owns reusable process bootstrap, security policy, ownership, Fx
# lifecycle, and managed listener generations. It is confined to command
# composition plus internal/bootstrap/sandbox, internal/app composition, and
# internal/runtime/listener; feature, platform, and transport code stay unaware
# of the lifecycle framework.
github.com/heavycaffeiner/hanami
github.com/heavycaffeiner/hanami/gin

# Fx is the explicit dependency-composition boundary. It is used only by cmd,
# bootstrap/sandbox, app composition, and runtime/listener; no feature or
# platform package may depend on it.
go.uber.org/fx

# Gin is the native HTTP router and handler context. The layer gate confines it
# to internal/transport/http, internal/app, and internal/runtime/listener.
github.com/gin-gonic/gin

# Argon2id password hashing, XChaCha20-Poly1305 at rest and MD4 for the SMB NT
# hash, none of which the standard library provides.
golang.org/x/crypto

# NFC/NFD handling and legacy code-page conversion tables.
golang.org/x/text

# ICU's character-set detector for non-UTF-8 archive names.
github.com/gogs/chardet

# SQLite translated to Go, keeping CGO_ENABLED=0 and static builds.
modernc.org/sqlite

# Pure-Go BLAKE3 for wire-visible directory and upload checksums.
lukechampine.com/blake3


# BMP, TIFF, and WebP decoding for preview workers.
golang.org/x/image

# Gorilla owns WebSocket upgrade, control frames, close codes, and
# fragmentation over native net/http.
github.com/gorilla/websocket
github.com/stowcloud/durablefs

# Standalone storage-neutral name search and SCNB v1 index.
github.com/stowcloud/namesearch

# Storage backends, transfer intervals and worker IPC are maintained as
# independent public modules. AWS and VeraCrypt are indirect storage dependencies.
github.com/stowcloud/storage
github.com/stowcloud/transfer
github.com/stowcloud/sandbox-worker
